# MCP server vetting checklist:
# 1. Source code available? (Is it open source?)
# 2. What does it claim to do vs what does the code actually do?
# 3. What filesystem/network access does it request?
# 4. Who maintains it? Individual or organization with track record?
# 5. How many installs/stars? (Community vetting signal)
# 6. Last updated? (Abandoned projects may have unpatched vulns)

# After vetting, install in .claude/mcp-settings.json with minimal permissions:
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "filesystem": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem", "./src"],
      # Scope to just ./src, not your entire filesystem
    }
  }
}
